From a36d8d251e183a25e2f67f9cb74a00c6dda9c893 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan B <bbigari@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:15:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Add AI Search Signals page

One page for "where do we show up in AI search", with the two kinds of
evidence kept visibly apart rather than blended into a single number.

The GA4 half is measured: Analytics recorded the referring host. It still
undercounts, because assistants that strip the referrer land in Direct, and
the card says so rather than implying a total. Filtering happens at Google on
a source regex so a large property does not need paging to surface a handful
of assistant rows.

The Search Console half is inferred: Google exposes no AI search type and no
AI searchAppearance, so the page matches query syntax people rarely type and
labels rows "Likely machine" or "Possible", never "AI". The regex used is
printed under the table so the inference is auditable, and the row links
through to Search Performance with the same filter applied.

Additive except for two nav registrations and the generated route tree, to
keep the next upstream merge small.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
